{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/974046-how-to-justify-enemys-not-having-silver-weaponry","id":974046,"title":"How to justify Enemys NOT having Silver Weaponry","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-21T14:57:09-07:00","id":974046,"title":"How to justify Enemys NOT having Silver Weaponry","content":"Silver in real life isnt that expensive, had some players bring that up (as well as &quot;How much silver is needed?&quot; and a cute idea of &quot;Silver frags shatters and each peice does an agg every turn right? <br /> <br /> but leaving all that aside, Idea on how to justify putting PC's against foes without silver weaponry, <br /> <br /> It suggests in W20 that the silver must be super pure, and that many jewelry silvers wont work.<br /> <br /> Any other ideas.on how to justify, Hunters, SAD Agents, or Pentex employees who arentt armed with Silver? <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T15:06:47-07:00","id":974053,"title":"","content":"Because fighting werewolves every day isn't a common occurrence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T15:08:02-07:00","id":974054,"title":"","content":"A few key things:<br /> <br /> 1) You have to know it works. What myths are and aren't true in the WoD are a jumble. Even with silver being true, it's not impossible to get conflicting reports on its effectiveness (since there are anti-silver Gifts).<br /> <br /> 2) It's not cheap. If you have backing sure, ~$5 a bullet isn't too harsh, but a lowly monster hunter is going to feel the pinch if they get into a serious fire-fight once or twice.<br /> <br /> 3) It's not subtle. Mostly for SAD agents, stockpiling silver risks members of outside agencies to get too curious.<br /> <br /> 4) You have werewolf bosses (Pentex with BSDs) who don't want you shooting them by mistake.<br /> <br /> 5) You don't actually want to kill the target, so non-agg is a better choice.<br /> <br /> 6) You have access to cheaper and easier to use agg damage (Pentex has plenty of choices).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T15:28:24-07:00","id":974065,"title":"","content":"7) You also need to know that simply silver-plating a bullet does <i>not</i> work. If you don't know that and observe that it doesn't work, you're (assuming you're human, or something akin to it) probably going to assume that the whole silver-and-werewolves thing is one of the pure bulls**t things in the World of Darkness (like the garlic-and-vampires thing).<br /> <br /> 8) Making silver bullets (well enough that they will actually work in a firearm and fly accurately) is not as simple as most people think. For instance, <a href=\"http://www.patriciabriggs.com/articles/silver/silverbullets.shtml\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.patriciabriggs.com/articl...rbullets.shtml</a> has a really fascinating article on this little issue. Also, silver bullets generally will not work in automatic action weapons (they induce stoppages).<br /> <br /> \u200bEDIT: I just realized that page three of that link has a reprint of a really funny <i>Gun World </i>magazine article from 1964 on firearms experts trying to recreate the Lone Ranger silver bullets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","user":"Uniform Two Six","date":". 09-21-2016, 08:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T15:33:31-07:00","id":974066,"title":"","content":"SAD is a government agency that is fairly underfunded. You are not requesitioning silver bullets. Pentex, the wyrm bites itself regularly these some accountant sees a requesition for &quot;Silver bullets&quot; gives into the temptation to just skim abit off the top and get them silver plated after all &quot;no one will notice because what the fuck werewolves aren't real!&quot;<br /> <br /> Its 5 dollars in raw materials. If the Hunter can make the bullets go right head, its just the hours spent making bullets are hours not doing other things. If he's getting them made by someone else? They could easily be 20 dollars a bullet, after all its a niche market where else are you going to buy silver bullets? And that's just for common shit like a 9mm. Good luck even trying to get someone to make a 50 cal silver bullet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T16:17:11-07:00","id":974091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/974046-how-to-justify-enemys-not-having-silver-weaponry?p=974066#post974066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">SAD is a government agency that is fairly underfunded. You are not requesitioning silver bullets...</div> </div> </div> </div>In Project Twilight, SAD agents actually <i>could</i> requisition silver bullets. The thing that always bothered me (given that I actually <i>have</i> some experience with government procurement), was <i>where</i> was the FBI going to requisition them <i>from</i>? Pretty sure there is no NSN# for silver bullets. That leaves them doing it in-house, which requires that you <i>seriously</i> know what you're doing, and even the Marine Corps gunsmiths at Quantico probably couldn't pull that one off.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T16:46:47-07:00","id":974110,"title":"","content":"Probaly have one or two Gunsmiths on site,to make them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T17:08:16-07:00","id":974120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/974046-how-to-justify-enemys-not-having-silver-weaponry?p=974054#post974054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) You have to know it works. What myths are and aren't true in the WoD are a jumble. Even with silver being true, it's not impossible to get conflicting reports on its effectiveness (since there are anti-silver Gifts).</div> </div> </div> </div>Furthermore, a &quot;werewolf&quot; for an uninformed human is a man that from one moment to the next become a &quot;wolf&quot; (not necessarily a Crinos, and if is a Crinos there's the Delirium to deal with...), and the Garou are not the only &quot;humans&quot; that turn to &quot;wolves&quot;, a lot of splats can do it.<br /> What if a noob hunter shoot a vampire in wolf-form (Gangrel, mainly) with silver bullets and don't get results?<br /> The 'wolf' will rip apart the team of the hunter and even if he survive, he will get the idea that the silver thing is only a fib. Given the fact that an hunter is more prone to stumble on vampires than on werewolves, it's a definite chance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T17:09:34-07:00","id":974122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/974046-how-to-justify-enemys-not-having-silver-weaponry?p=974110#post974110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probaly have one or two Gunsmiths on site,to make them.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bYeah, only that even at the SAD's height in the 1950s, they never had more than 50 people working there. With a staff of only a dozen or two, the one or two gunsmiths (and the metallurgist you'd need to figure out all of the quirks of casting silver to the tolerances needed to <i>not</i> have the gun be more dangerous to the shooter than to the werewolf), would in and of itself represent a huge percentage of the SAD's manpower.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T17:30:37-07:00","id":974132,"title":"","content":"Or you don't try to justify it, and the players start learning the value of Dodging, Cover, and *egad!* actually using their heads and making plans and team work","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T17:39:57-07:00","id":974135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/974046-how-to-justify-enemys-not-having-silver-weaponry?p=974091#post974091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Project Twilight, SAD agents actually <i>could</i> requisition silver bullets. The thing that always bothered me (given that I actually <i>have</i> some experience with government procurement), was <i>where</i> was the FBI going to requisition them <i>from</i>? Pretty sure there is no NSN# for silver bullets. That leaves them doing it in-house, which requires that you <i>seriously</i> know what you're doing, and even the Marine Corps gunsmiths at Quantico probably couldn't pull that one off.</div> </div> </div> </div>And they still can in HH2, but in modern times, they're referred to as Code Five rounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T17:43:53-07:00","id":974137,"title":"","content":"I imagine that even foes who know about werewolves and know that silver hurts them won't necessarily be expecting to fight werewolves at any given moment. So a bunch of Pentex agents who are going on a mission to kill werewolves would almost certainly have silver weapons or something else designed to kill werewolves. But, if those same agents are out and about, potentially expected no trouble or maybe some more mundane issue, and they may not have silver bullets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T17:50:10-07:00","id":974140,"title":"","content":"The problem is that you cannot easily mass produce silver rounds. Bullet molds for home assume lead bullets, and they will cracking or warp if molten silver is poured in them. In effect, you would have to use a specially mold (probably tungsten given the temperatures) to mass produce silver rounds. Mass producing silver sabot rounds would require a factory because sabot round are difficult to make (at least ten minutes each if you are doing it by hand and know what you are doing). If a gunsmith had the right equipment, they might be able to fill a clip with silver bullets in a couple of hours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T18:22:17-07:00","id":974155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/974046-how-to-justify-enemys-not-having-silver-weaponry?p=974140#post974140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that you cannot easily mass produce silver rounds. Bullet molds for home assume lead bullets, and they will cracking or warp if molten silver is poured in them. In effect, you would have to use a specially mold (probably tungsten given the temperatures) to mass produce silver rounds. Mass producing silver sabot rounds would require a factory because sabot round are difficult to make (at least ten minutes each if you are doing it by hand and know what you are doing). If a gunsmith had the right equipment, they might be able to fill a clip with silver bullets in a couple of hours.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure that some group with resources and technical knowledge could mass produce silver bullets - like Pentex. Companies don't have any trouble mass producing things made of steel. <br /> <br /> An amateur gunsmith would have more trouble. I think if I were going to try to make silver bullets for a rifled gun, I would use silver cylinders and a metal lathe to create bullets of the right size so that thermal expansion doesn't leave us with bullets that are smaller than the cast and pitting from high temperature oxidation wouldn't be an issue either. In that case, the labor would be worth more than the price of silver bullion. <br /> <br /> Of course, the easy thing would be to get some silver chain and break it into links and then pack it into a shotgun shell. Even a silver slug would be a lot more forgiving than bullets for rifled firearms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T18:24:41-07:00","id":974156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/974046-how-to-justify-enemys-not-having-silver-weaponry?p=974140#post974140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...In effect, you would have to use a specially mold (probably tungsten given the temperatures) to mass produce silver rounds...</div> </div> </div> </div> It turns out, special mold: yes. Special material: no. Good old fashioned steel works. One of the biggest problems is that silver has a melting point somewhere north of 1600F. This requires that the mold be heated to a nearly equally insane temperature to allow for a smooth casting without imperfections forming from uneven cooling. Silver also has a peculiarly large discrepancy in volume when heated so if you pour molten silver into a mold, it will come out of the mold significantly smaller than the mold itself. This is complicated by the fact that the mold (if properly heated as above) will also expand to a degree, meaning that in order for the rounds to be the proper size for the weapon's bore diameter (so it doesn't just blow up in your hands), you actually have to do some <i>seriously</i> complicated calculations to figure out just what the interior diameter (and other dimensions) of your mold need to be before your start heating them in a furnace. Also, making sure that your mold is heated to the right temperature is also a factor.<br /> <br /> Seriously. Read the article. It's hilarious.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T18:25:08-07:00","id":974157,"title":"","content":"On SAD something else ive wondered about, ideas on how to incorporate them into a mixed hunters group<br /> <br /> I see two possibletys<br /> <br /> the SAD , Reluctantly sees that desperate times breed desperate measures.<br /> <br /> or he's infiltrating a group of civilian hunters, to see how competent or dangerous they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" bord