rget=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 09-24-2016, 09:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T16:10:57-07:00","id":975725,"title":"","content":"The Mythbusters also did a little messing around with Silver Bullets (testing the Lone Ranger's calling card). Even if a Garou-hating hunter made the custom molds and equipment to make silver bullets... lightweight silver makes for a terrible projectile. Because physics. <a href=\"http://www.discovery.com/tv-shows/mythbusters/videos/silver-vs-lead-bullets/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.discovery.com/tv-shows/my...-lead-bullets/</a><br /> <br /> Based on that test, silver bullets should have a pretty significant damage penalty. Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T18:11:38-07:00","id":975753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crusher-of-Cities</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/974046-how-to-justify-enemys-not-having-silver-weaponry?p=975725#post975725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Mythbusters also did a little messing around with Silver Bullets (testing the Lone Ranger's calling card). Even if a Garou-hating hunter made the custom molds and equipment to make silver bullets... lightweight silver makes for a terrible projectile. Because physics. <a href=\"http://www.discovery.com/tv-shows/mythbusters/videos/silver-vs-lead-bullets/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.discovery.com/tv-shows/my...-lead-bullets/</a><br /> <br /> Based on that test, silver bullets should have a pretty significant damage penalty. Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>That isn't true. Silver is only slightly lighter than lead. The reasons that the Mythbuster silver bullets didn't work were more complex, read the Patricia Briggs link and it explains the issues. Basically, the Mythbusters didn't make very good bullets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T23:40:25-07:00","id":975858,"title":"","content":"To hurt werewolves the bullet doesn't need to be all by silver, but only the cover, and the origin about silver againts werewolves is because the beast of G\u00e9vaudan (a strange predator from real life) was killed by the Jean Chaster, with a bulltet <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">from </span></span><span style=\"color:#6A6A6A\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>silver </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">medals depicting the </span></span><span style=\"color:#6A6A6A\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Virgin</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"> Mary and blessed by the local </span></span>priest.<br /> <br /> And maybe werewolves can endurace organic toxins, but not acid sustances like brumine, or sulfur. They background about licantropes can be changed totally and for example they could be allergic to cupper and mercury.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":11152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","user":"Luis Carlos","date":". 09-25-2016, 02:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T00:00:25-07:00","id":975860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/974046-how-to-justify-enemys-not-having-silver-weaponry?p=975858#post975858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To hurt werewolves the bullet doesn't need to be all by silver, but only the cover, and the origin about silver againts werewolves is because the beast of G\u00e9vaudan (a strange predator from real life) was killed by the Jean Chaster, with a bulltet <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">from </span></span><span style=\"color:#6A6A6A\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>silver </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">medals depicting the </span></span><span style=\"color:#6A6A6A\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Virgin</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"> Mary and blessed by the local </span></span>priest.<br /> <br /> And maybe werewolves can endurace organic toxins, but not acid sustances like brumine, or sulfur. They background about licantropes can be changed totally and for example they could be allergic to cupper.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an interesting origin for the silver bullet legend.<br /> <br /> Really, there are numerous ways to make incredibly dangerous silver bullets. Something like this <a href=\"https://www.gunsamerica.com/blog/drt-frangible-223-ammo-vs-charging-wild-boar/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.gunsamerica.com/blog/drt...ing-wild-boar/</a> but with powdered silver inside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T02:45:12-07:00","id":975891,"title":"","content":"I think changing the rules of the game (even if to fit various real world mythologies better) is a bit off the point of how to handle silver in the game as is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T07:02:52-07:00","id":975931,"title":"","content":"Silver coating should not be allowed for bullets because bullets mushroom and deform when they hit (and silver coating would be peeled off by any rifling anyway). After all, silver coating does not make knives do aggravated damage, and the knife would actually keep the coating for a few attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T08:05:02-07:00","id":975945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/974046-how-to-justify-enemys-not-having-silver-weaponry?p=975931#post975931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Silver coating should not be allowed for bullets because bullets mushroom and deform when they hit (and silver coating would be peeled off by any rifling anyway). After all, silver coating does not make knives do aggravated damage, and the knife would actually keep the coating for a few attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, it can make knives do aggravated damage, but only once or twice before the coating wears away. Mokole, though vulnerable to both silver and gold, however, have a passage that explicitly states that just coating a weapon won't do it, and that it will come right off on their scaly hides to no effect (except to make the Mokole know that you know too much and should be killed).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T08:36:22-07:00","id":975954,"title":"","content":"I have always thought that maybe the should be some kind of middle ground for weapons which include some silver but that aren't completely silver. Maybe, just as an example, a silver coated bullet does one point of unsoakable aggravated damage but the rest is normal. Or perhaps they could inflict aggravated damage but it is soakable. Something like that. I wouldn't necessarily rely on the silver plating coming off, because that depends on how thick the plating is and how it was applied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T14:08:25-07:00","id":976088,"title":"","content":"It's mentioned in several places (I want to say the Storytellers' Handbook, but I don't have my books with me at the moment), that silver-plating does <i>not</i> work -- at all. Now as mentioned before, full-silver projectiles will induce stoppages in automatics. In my weredog sourcebook I'm putting together, this creates a problem (since the weredogs can't create -- or even attune -- Klaives). For the most part, they use lever-action, bolt-action, and pump-action weapons to get around this issue, but for situations where that's not a option, I came up with rules for (what I'm calling) &quot;partially-jacketed silver&quot; rounds. These are basically the things on the last page of the Patricia Briggs article. Basically, they work like normal ammunition, only after rolling damage, you annotate half of the damage (rounded down, but with a minimum of one die) as silver damage, with the rest normal non-aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> So if you hit a werewolf for three dice, one die is considered silver (one-half of three, rounded down), and can<i>not</i> be soaked by Garou, and the other two are normal lethal damage, <i>can</i> be soaked <i>and</i> regenerated.<br /> <br /> If you hit him for only one die, that die (since it's a minimum of one) is considered silver.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","user":"Uniform Two Six","date":". 09-25-2016, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T14:19:48-07:00","id":976096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/974046-how-to-justify-enemys-not-having-silver-weaponry?p=975954#post975954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have always thought that maybe the should be some kind of middle ground for weapons which include some silver but that aren't completely silver. Maybe, just as an example, a silver coated bullet does one point of unsoakable aggravated damage but the rest is normal. Or perhaps they could inflict aggravated damage but it is soakable. Something like that. I wouldn't necessarily rely on the silver plating coming off, because that depends on how thick the plating is and how it was applied.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much every answer on this has been published at some point. Some books say silver plating works fine. Others say isn't enough at it has to be &quot;physically and spiritually pure&quot; silver. One book says silver nitrate is deadly, another says it does nothing. Some books have silver alloy weapons that deal soakable agg, others agg soakable at dif 8. Authors have had virtually zero consistency, even mid-edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T17:52:41-07:00","id":976193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crusher-of-Cities</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/974046-how-to-justify-enemys-not-having-silver-weaponry?p=976096#post976096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty much every answer on this has been published at some point. Some books say silver plating works fine. Others say isn't enough at it has to be &quot;physically and spiritually pure&quot; silver. One book says silver nitrate is deadly, another says it does nothing. Some books have silver alloy weapons that deal soakable agg, others agg soakable at dif 8. Authors have had virtually zero consistency, even mid-edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Silver nitrate hollow points were before revised. There was a standard in revised (refer to the thin book that came with the ST screen) that got carried over into W20, where plating or coating will wear off quickly but act as a silver weapon, and relatively high silver content alloys will irritate a Garou.but not do aggravated damage, and you need something on the order of 9/10ths purity or else it's just going to sting a bit more than usual.<br /> <br /> Then someone decided that they just had to have the silver nitrate hollow points back in the fucking game with W20 Book of the Wyrm, and just called them something different, but just as bogus a reason for their existence. Argh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T18:00:41-07:00","id":976197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/974046-how-to-justify-enemys-not-having-silver-weaponry?p=975860#post975860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is an interesting origin for the silver bullet legend.<br /> <br /> Really, there are numerous ways to make incredibly dangerous silver bullets. Something like this <a href=\"https://www.gunsamerica.com/blog/drt-frangible-223-ammo-vs-charging-wild-boar/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.gunsamerica.com/blog/drt...ing-wild-boar/</a> but with powdered silver inside.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, since it's come up...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Silver coating should not be allowed for bullets because bullets mushroom and deform when they hit (and silver coating would be peeled off by any rifling anyway). After all, silver coating does not make knives do aggravated damage, and the knife would actually keep the coating for a few attacks. </div> </div> </div>Here's the rub. Jacketing a round in silver is the exact opposite way to do it; you'd want to jacket a silver <i>penetrator</i>. You overcome all the aforementioned issues with casting and metal shrinkage, retain ballistic properties, but with <i>lower overall </i>penetration which is precisely what you want against a werewolf (overpenetration being the worst-case scenario, you want the round <i>still inside</i> the werewolf, continuing to do damage).<br /> <br /> The absolute gold standard as far as I could surmise, would be a tungsten-jacketed, silver-cored, hollow point with a center-post (i.e. the &quot;Hydra-Shok&quot;) design. Good luck getting your hands on <i>that</i> without being a highly-skilled gunsmith with high Resources and access to the necessary equipment that would allow you to work with tungsten, though.<br /> <br /> Although frankly, silver rifle rounds aren't the way you'd want to go, anyhow. You want <b><i>shotguns</i></b>. Silver shot, silver flechettes, hell I once saw a video where someone successfully made an APFSDS (armor-piercing fin-stabilized discarding sabot, in other words the same design as a contemporary AP <i>tank round</i>) round for a 12-ga. Or hell, if you're my aforementioned sorcerer, go for the motherfucking gold. 12-ga. HEAT rounds which use silver as the penetrator, opposed to copper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T20:00:24-07:00","id":976290,"title":"","content":"Or you could do a shape charge effect with a LAW, but replace the normal metal tip and liner with silver, so the 'jet' is high velocity super heated silver dust followed by a lower velocity super heated 'slug'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T00:50:45-07:00","id":977050,"title":"","content":"Maybe there is another secret way to hurt Garou, with bones by Black Spiral Dancers (or even from kindred corpses), or bones from some mystic beast or spirit. Or by metal got from some spirit realms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T16:14:29-07:00","id":977458,"title":"","content":"And that would be easier for mortal hunters to gain access to how?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T01:28:14-07:00","id":977658,"title":"","content":"The easiest solution for silver weapons is the shotgun. Shotguns are designed to fire pellets and once a suitable amount of silver has been melted and turned into pellets normal re-loading equipment would suffice. Now will every hunter, ghoul, mage acolyte have silver of course not.<br /> Cases where silver is reasonable:<br /> Pentex First team- requisitioned and only if the threat is confirmed. Example: Garou have attacked the Endron oil refinery in Newark, NJ twice in a 6 month period the guards and First Team tasked with protecting/hunting down the pack or packs responsible will be issued special rounds.<br /> Ghouls where the threat of Garou action against a vampire is high. Example: There have been a number of attacks in a city on Vampires the Vampires suspect Garou are responsible the wealthier Vampires hand out silver rounds to there Ghoul Bodyguards.<br /> Cults/Acolytes this one is a stretch unless the Garou are attacking a Mage Chantry/Construct and the Mages have used whatever you choose to warn them.<br /> &quot;Normal Hunters&quot; most Werewolf hunters* are Kin and probably going to go for silver for the purpose of skinning...<br /> As for organized groups play it by ear and make it rational.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T09:12:47-07:00","id":977800,"title":"","content":"Another option is to be hurt by weapons forged or created with supernatural creatures' blood. Or armor-piercing shell or HEAT (high-explosive anti-tank warhead), or hollow-point bullets. I guess molten metal can hurt werebeast enough.<br /> <br /> My opinion is only silver can hurt garous with direct contact and doesn't allow regeneration, but they can be hurt during fights by another ways. Normal weapons can hurt garous, but it is harder to cause bigger injuries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T13:24:41-07:00","id":978574,"title":"","content":"Silver weapons, by the power of physics, should be weaker. I suppose to some extent this is replicated in game: A Grand Klaive does +3 silver damage, difficulty 7. A battle axe does something like difficulty 7, +6 damage. The silver weapons on the melee table perform univerally perform worse than non-silver counterparts, even if we ignore bullshit claymores. Silver is a (relatively) soft metal, and even when garou make klaives with it and do some magical spiritual strengthening on the steel, they still need to make short and thick blades to give it more strength. Using silver will inevitably give you decreased damage and/or increased difficulty. <br /> <br /> For guns. Increased difficulty doesn't make much sense, but you're going to do decreased damage. There isn't rules for this, so maybe invent some. Like +1 difficulty to damage dice, Or a percentage less damage. Or reduced soak if they can soak it. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T13:33:25-07:00","id":978583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/974046-how-to-justify-enemys-not-having-silver-weaponry?p=978574#post978574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Silver weapons, by the power of physics, should be weaker. I suppose to some extent this is replicated in game: A Grand Klaive does +3 silver damage, difficulty 7. A battle axe does something like difficulty 7, +6 damage. The silver weapons on the melee table perform univerally perform worse than non-silver counterparts, even if we ignore bullshit claymores. Silver is a (relatively) soft metal, and even when garou make klaives with it and do some magical spiritual strengthening on the steel, they still need to make short and thick blades to give it more strength. Using silver will inevitably give you decreased damage and/or increased difficulty.<br /> <br /> For guns. Increased difficulty doesn't make much sense, but you're going to do decreased damage. There isn't rules for this, so maybe invent some. Like +1 difficulty to damage dice, Or a percentage less damage. Or reduced soak if they can soak it.</div> </div> </div> </div>As of W20, per the table on page 302, a grand klaive does Strength +5, while a great axe is only one die beyond it and requires Strength 3+ to wield (which a grand klaive does not), suggesting that they are, once one takes the greater weight into account, about equal. Then again, a grand klaive has been treated with a magical process to make its silver composition the equal of steel, so it's not really a comparison that works.<br /> <br /> (Also, going back to the book that came with the W:tA Revised ST screen, silver weapons or ammo did one less die of damage).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T13:52:54-07:00","id":978598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/974046-how-to-justify-enemys-not-having-silver-weaponry?p=978574#post978574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Silver weapons, by the power of physics, should be weaker. I suppose to some extent this is replicated in game: A Grand Klaive does +3 silver damage, difficulty 7. A battle axe does something like difficulty 7, +6 damage. The silver weapons on the melee table perform univerally perform worse than non-silver counterparts, even if we ignore bullshit claymores. Silver is a (relatively) soft metal, and even when garou make klaives with it and do some magical spiritual strengthening on the steel, they still need to make short and thick blades to give it more strength. Using silver will inevitably give you decreased damage and/or increased difficulty.<br /> <br /> For guns. Increased difficulty doesn't make much sense, but you're going to do decreased damage. There isn't rules for this, so maybe invent some. Like +1 difficulty to damage dice, Or a percentage less damage. Or reduced soak if they can soak it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that this is an oversimplification and overestimating the softness of silver. With a weapon like a mace, hammer, or axe there should be no functional difference between that and a steel version - except that it will likely need to be sharpened or repaired more often. A sword made of silver would be nearly unusable because of the extreme weight of silver. Silver melee weapons need to be those that have longer shafts and smaller metal parts that that the weight isn't too great. As for bullets, they may do slightly less damage as they effectively act as armor piercing rounds - silver being so much harder than lead. Maybe one die less, though I might actually give them a bonus to penetrate a vest. With some silver bullets, like silver shot, there should be no difference in damage between them and standard shot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T14:02:07-07:00","id":978603,"title":"","content":"Incorrect. On 302 of W20, A great axe is dif 7 (with the min strength rule, which the majority of garou pass), +6. A Grand klaive is dif 7 +3<br /> <br /> <br /> One die less of damage is silly, because it doesn't work in proportion to the weapon. One less dice on a .50 BMG doesn't mean anything, when in reality it'd impact the performance of the weapon more significantly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T14:08:53-07:00","id":978611,"title":"","content":"Well, the dice system can't represent really small changes. Maybe for a really powerful round, like a .50 BMG, might have -2 dice instead of -1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T15:42:14-07:00","id":978677,"title":"","content":"It would not cause less damage though, when you get to large rounds, because the wound channel would be similar in size (large rounds with high velocities, like a .50 BMG, tend to overpenetrate anything less tough than a couple of inches of steel before mushrooming and tumbling). That is why a .50 BMG round can go through a few houses and a dozen innocent bystanders before it stops.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T15:54:32-07:00","id":978686,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm not sure where I stand on that exactly. I have heard good arguments for and against a silver .50 BMG doing less damage. The round would be moving so fast that it could potentially transfer a lot of energy, but over penetration is a thing which is why they make a variety of bullets to prevent that - like hollow tips. <br /> <br /> One option may be something like this: <a href=\"https://www.gunsamerica.com/blog/drt-frangible-223-ammo-vs-charging-wild-boar/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.gunsamerica.com/blog/drt...ing-wild-boar/</a><br /> <br /> Frangible hunting rounds. Instead of the metallic power that a normal round like this has, replace it with condensed silver dust.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T17:12:20-07:00","id":978730,"title":"","content":"You are not going to find conventional hollow points for .50 BMG (and hollow point or frangible rounds are not a good idea for high velocity rounds, they tend to shatter due to the force of the explosion of the round).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T17:52:07-07:00","id":978742,"title":"","content":"That is true. I guess that somebody with a lot of resources (Pentex, for example) could make them. Though they do have frangible .223 or .308 ammo which is going to be useful as well, even if it doesn't pack the same punch as a .50 BMG. I have discussed .50 BMG sabots before and they should work pretty well, and will be going insanely fast when they strike the target, which might cause nasty hydrostatic shock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T18:28:03-07:00","id":978757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/974046-how-to-justify-enemys-not-having-silver-weaponry?p=978603#post978603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incorrect. On 302 of W20, A great axe is dif 7 (with the min strength rule, which the majority of garou pass), +6. A Grand klaive is dif 7 +3</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't seem like something they'd just up and change from the November 2013 version of the pdf, and that's the one I'm citing. I'm zooming in, it isn't an ambiguous case by strained eyes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One die less of damage is silly, because it doesn't work in proportion to the weapon. One less dice on a .50 BMG doesn't mean anything, when in reality it'd impact the performance of the weapon more significantly. </div> </div> </div>That may be why it didn't make it into W20. Still, the game has approached the stand point of &quot;silver is not good for making weapons&quot; in the past, and it could conceivably do it again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T20:02:54-07:00","id":978803,"title":"","content":"Hm, a silver kusari would be a good weapon against a Garou, and it would not be any less effective than a normal kusari. It could also be hidden as an ornate belt outside of combat, but it could be quickly deployed. In real life, it would be a difficult weapon to use, but it would be comparable to a flail when it comes to damage, but it would have greater range and can entangle an opponent. A Garou trapped by a silver kusari would not be happy with the experience. I think a reasonable price for a silver kusari would be around $2,000, since a 'standard' kusari is around 80 ounces in weight (which would be $1,600 in silver)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T20:14:33-07:00","id":978813,"title":"","content":"I would go for a spear. The No.1 weapon of man. Also, Gloriously cheap. <br /> Or an assault rifle. The No.1 weapon of modern man<br /> If we discount knifes of course. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T21:08:36-07:00","id":978835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/974046-how-to-justify-enemys-not-having-silver-weaponry?p=978803#post978803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, a silver kusari would be a good weapon against a Garou, and it would not be any less effective than a normal kusari. It could also be hidden as an ornate belt outside of combat, but it could be quickly deployed. In real life, it would be a difficult weapon to use, but it would be comparable to a flail when it comes to damage, but it would have greater range and can entangle an opponent. A Garou trapped by a silver kusari would not be happy with the experience. I think a reasonable price for a silver kusari would be around $2,000, since a 'standard' kusari is around 80 ounces in weight (which would be $1,600 in silver)</div> </div> </div> </div>Who the hell makes thick-linked chains of silver, with the possibility of putting a silver farm implement on the end, other than Shih? That's going to be eminently noticeable and weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T15:34:49-07:00","id":982401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/974046-how-to-justify-enemys-not-having-silver-weaponry?p=978742#post978742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have discussed .50 BMG sabots before and they should work pretty well, and will be going insanely fast when they strike the target, which might cause nasty hydrostatic shock.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, .50 cal sabots would do nothing appreciably better in this instance. They're anti-materiel rounds, not anti-personnel. If I remember my ballistics right, they transfer a lot less force to the target and produce pathetic wound channels compared to same-caliber anti-personnel rounds. They'd probably perform <i>worse</i>, taking that into consideration.<br /> <br /> Hydrostatic shock I doubt would even be a consideration against garou, considering their tremendous toughness and healing factor. Maybe if they're in lupus or homid form, but I doubt the hybrid forms or crinos would be even worth discussing.<br /> <br /> If you want any kind of armor-penetrating round at all, you'll want to go smoothbore (i.e. shotguns). Likewise, as I said, any discussion of jacketed rounds or super-high calibers is the wrong way to go. You <i>don't</i> want overpenetration; the ideal situation is the round doesn't through and through, instead staying in the werewolf's body continuing to cause damage on a per-turn basis as any contact with silver would, nerfing their Gnosis as potentially forcing them back into breed form for the sake of survival. Jacketed hollowpoints and semi-wadcutters really is the way to go, here, and as a ballpark I'd say nothing higher caliber than .30-06.<br /> <br /> And, as a semi-postscript, I have my doubts about silver bullets being perfectly usable in semi-autos and autos. Silver <i>is</i> a lighter metal, and one would need to increase the powder charge commensurately to get comparable ballistic performance (provided they're hand-loading, or mass producing custom rounds). At least, it may make for <i>unreliable</i> performance in recoil-operated systems, and considering the need to increase the powder charge, blowback- or gas-operated may be the way to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T15:55:31-07:00","id":982411,"title":"","content":"Silver is 92% the density of lead and 130% denser than steel, the two most common materials for bullets. It will outperform steel for wounding and lead for penetration, so it would be the ideal round because it is soft enough to tumble in flesh (rather than mushrooming like lead or penetrating like steel) while it is hard enough to penetrate most ballistic armors. As for .50 caliber, who cares? Garou might as well be human when hit by a silver round, and humans do not survive a body shot from .50 BMG. They should die with a sizzling hole the size of a bowling ball in their torso and revert to their breed form. Also, you do not need more powder for a lighter round, the increased velocity from the same powder charge should balance out the change in kinetic energy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T16:34:55-07:00","id":982429,"title":"","content":"The reason I mentioned a .50 BMG sabot isn't because I think that the sabot would be better, but because it would solve what ever issues there are with silver bullets and rifling. Like Aya Tari says, a .50 cal is super lethal anyway. I think that a silver frangible bullet might be the thing to go with. Design it the same way as you would design a frangible hunting round but replace the inside with silver powder. Silver isn't that much lighter than lead, the density is fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T08:05:03-07:00","id":984404,"title":"","content":"Aside from the usefulness of silver rounds, one factor that may limit their use for hunters without unlimited budgets is that hypothetically, in the WoD, silver might be more expensive than the real world. In a world with actual werewolves (and thus actual werewolf hunters) and organizations like Pentex buying silver for strike teams (and perhaps as a middleman for supplying materials for BSD klaives), that both theoretically increases demand and reduces supply. It might not be a huge uptick in price, but over time it adds up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T13:29:02-07:00","id":984577,"title":"","content":"Why? It is not like the existence of Garou is common knowledge, the vast majority of people really do not believe in Werewolves, and the world produces over 26 million ounces of silver every year. That translates to over 150 lbs of silver per year per Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T14:56:10-07:00","id":984607,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the industrial uses of silver in manufacturing alone are going to<i> massively </i>outweigh the (relatively) tiny volumes used for anything related to werewolves. Unless Pentex has a warehouse the size of a high school gymnasium, chock-full to the rafters with nothing but silver, the price of a troy ounce isn't going to move a tick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T15:12:12-07:00","id":984613,"title":"","content":"Silver is too expensive to be used for bullets. Silver blades can be created and be used by generations for centuries. Yes, a silver weapon would be expensive like a house, but that worth it. Supernatural creatures don't need silver, Normal soldiers can hurt werewolves with incendiary or explosive bullets. Silver is better, but with the same money you can buy enough ammuntion to cause the same damage. Let's say it is qualty vs quanty.<br /> <br /> Normal agents (FBI, CIA, S.W.A.T, police) will not use silver weapons, the main reason because supernatural creatures is a hidden secret, (the true challenge for garous isn't killing humans, but to avoid be discovered) and technocracy covered agents don't need silver because they have their own &quot;cheap&quot; ways to hurt freaks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T15:48:56-07:00","id":984627,"title":"","content":"Even Garou in Crinos form are not going to enjoy being targeted by incendiary .50 BMG rounds from a sniper rifle and, what is really great, it will work equally well against nearly every type of supernatural creature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T00:17:24-07:00","id":984773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/974046-how-to-justify-enemys-not-having-silver-weaponry?p=984627#post984627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even Garou in Crinos form are not going to enjoy being targeted by incendiary .50 BMG rounds from a sniper rifle and, what is really great, it will work equally well against nearly every type of supernatural creature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on who operates the gun though because of things like Delirium, Revelation (and possibly other such things for other creature types)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T08:45:29-07:00","id":984896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/974046-how-to-justify-enemys-not-having-silver-weaponry?p=984627#post984627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even Garou in Crinos form are not going to enjoy being targeted by incendiary .50 BMG rounds from a sniper rifle and, what is really great, it will work equally well against nearly every type of supernatural creature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Master of Fire says no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T09:16:15-07:00","id":984910,"title":"","content":"Also... regardless of the various books' attempts to stat up such things, a high powered incendiary around against a flesh and blood target is pretty pointless. This is something where over penetration really matters beyond much dispute: burning things generally takes time, which means an incendiary that just passes right through a target without stopping will do nothing more than a normal bullet.<br /> <br /> This is another situation like silver where a slower moving projectile is generally preferable because even more than silver and its magical interaction with Garou, an incendiary round needs the right conditions to actually burn things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T04:20:21-07:00","id":987186,"title":"","content":"As a random on-topic reference calculation, a 00 Buckshot shell filled with around 15 pellets of 999 fine silver would cost, minimum, around 28 dollars per shell.<br /> 8.38mm diameter per pellet equals a volume of 308.13mm\u00b3,<br /> which means each pellet weights about 3.235 grams (0.114 ounces),<br /> times 15 means 48.525 grams (1.712 ounces),<br /> which means a rough price of 27.25 dollars for the whole payload. Not counting gunpowder, shell plastic, primer, profit calculations by the silver suppler and manufacturing of the whole ready shell.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> Even with 925 Sterling, the price would be around 25 dollars, still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 10-14-2016, 07:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T05:29:31-07:00","id":987204,"title":"","content":"Silver may be the best way to hurt garous, but it isn't the only way. Silver is too expensive to be used for bullets, supernatural enemies have got their own ways to hurt garous, and ordinary agents only would use silve only if they know about garous and they are about to face someone.<br /> <br /> Maybe a garou could be surprised because he has been hurt by a normal weapon, and he doesn't notice really this arms has been blessed/cursed/charmed by a wraiht who wants revenge. .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T07:48:34-07:00","id":987252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/974046-how-to-justify-enemys-not-having-silver-weaponry?p=987204#post987204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Silver may be the best way to hurt garous, but it isn't the only way. Silver is too expensive to be used for bullets, supernatural enemies have got their own ways to hurt garous, and ordinary agents only would use silve only if they know about garous and they are about to face someone.<br /> <br /> Maybe a garou could be surprised because he has been hurt by a normal weapon, and he doesn't notice really this arms has been blessed/cursed/charmed by a wraiht who wants revenge. .</div> </div> </div> </div>Wraiths that can do that can usually just act on the material world themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T08:22:50-07:00","id":987266,"title":"","content":"Supernatural creatures can find the unpleasant surprise they are the fetters of the humans they killed in the past. A straightfowar relation between killer and victim isn't necesary, only to be in the same faction. A wraith for example could hate not only the Lasombra Sabath vampire who killed him, but all vampires in the general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T08:30:48-07:00","id":987267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/974046-how-to-justify-enemys-not-having-silver-weaponry?p=987204#post987204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Silver is too expensive to be used for bullets</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree for the most part, and it's why I did the rough calculation of the price of a shotgun shell above/below.<br /> <br /> However I can see how normal folk still would get their hands on (pricy and rare) bullets or shells like that: Pentex.<br /> <br /> It's documented that Pentex has silver bullets, and while the books mostly talk about those being used potentially by First Teams or on Endron oil rigs, I totally can see Pentex seeding certain black markets with a limited supply of those bullets and the traders who sell them and the according stories along the lines of 'Hey, if you have problems with, you know..those things..I've got something for you'.<br /> <br /> Why?<br /> Revenge-driven fanatic folk who lost family members to the shifters and remember it despite the delirium, monster hunters, etc. etc.<br /> Sure, small market, but people will pay an arm and a leg for those shells in their desparation. That just means more profits for Pentex, and potentially a few dead shifters. Outside of that though, I don't really see the chance to cross the trajectory of a silver bullet as even mediocre.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 10-14-2016, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T10:19:41-07:00","id":987323,"title":"","content":"Silver can be used by Pentex elite special forces, and maybe the fomorians can get silver in their own mines in umbral realm, but normal fomorian have got their own ways to hurt garous. Maybe the bones of Black Spiral Dancers and kinkfolk can be used for ammunition, and tainted quicksilver.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T19:20:13-07:00","id":987547,"title":"","content":"Silver is actually pretty cheap. Loading your gun with silver bullets is going to be cheaper than the expense of buying the gun, at least the value of the actual silver. If you're going into a fight with such a powerful creature, and exploiting its weakness just costs you a few hundred dollars, you do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T19:43:38-07:00","id":987559,"title":"","content":"Silver might be cheap, but decent silver ammunition is quite rare and expensive. Anyone can make an improvised load of silver shot for a shotgun, but it will not be as effective or as damaging as a real ammunition. While it will likely be effective against Garou, the vast majority of people will not be able to tell a Garou from a normal human being until it is too late, and I think that a would-be werewolf hunter would feel really stupid if they wasted a few hundred dollars to kill normal human beings (plus it would be like leaving a calling card for the police).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T07:59:06-07:00","id":987751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/974046-how-to-justify-enemys-not-having-silver-weaponry?p=987547#post987547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Silver is actually pretty cheap. Loading your gun with silver bullets is going to be cheaper than the expense of buying the gun, at least the value of the actual silver. If you're going into a fight with such a powerful creature, and exploiting its weakness just costs you a few hundred dollars, you do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cheap is relative. As I wrote in my post, the actual silver content in a single 00 buck shell would be around 30 dollars alone to get, without accounting for the rest of the materials, or making the whole thing (or getting it made). Per shot. Not counting anything else.<br /> You're looking at at least 300+ dollars for 10 shells. And no person or group actively hunting Garou is going to get far with just a few of those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T09:26:37-07:00","id":987793,"title":"","content":"Bullets don't need to be totally by silver, but only the surface. Within projectile can be made by another material. And the bullet hasn't to be totally pure silver.<br /> <br /> Silver is too expensive for automatic firearms, but for a profesional sniper only a bullet may be worth.<br /> <br /> I would bet Pentex has got its own supernatural ways to find silver mines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T10:42:43-07:00","id":987824,"title":"","content":"Bullets have to be pure silver though, as the silver on the surface of the bullet would be peeled off by rifling or by the mushrooming of the bullet. A silver plated bullet would, at best, increase the difficulty of soaking the lethal damage from '6' to '7'. And you do not need to find new silver mines, we produce over 33,000 metric tons of silver per year globally (gold production is over 3,000 metric tons per year globally by comparison), it is just that the demand for silver in industry and jewelry keeps the price so high.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T15:50:29-07:00","id":987972,"title":"","content":"Pentex, and the Silver fangs or glasswalkers probaly try to keep control of a mine or two, nonetheless just to be on the safeside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T18:13:53-07:00","id":988034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/974046-how-to-justify-enemys-not-having-silver-weaponry?p=987793#post987793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bullets don't need to be totally by silver, but only the surface. Within projectile can be made by another material. And the bullet hasn't to be totally pure silver.</div> </div> </div> </div>This topic was beaten to death 3 pages ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T04:59:33-07:00","id":988792,"title":"","content":"I have readen the rules, and bullets covered with silver can hurt, but all weapons covered with silver lose it after a couple of hits. Garous also can be hurt with natural weapons of supernatural enemies (fangs, claws, horns, spikes...). And Pentex can raise a &quot;farm&quot; of poisonous &quot;pokemons&quot;. <br /> <br /> Other option is ordinary agentes to be equipped with &quot;special weapons&quot; like bullets of &quot;frozen poison&quot; or &quot;poisonous ice&quot; but they don't know they are using &quot;technomagic&quot;,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T08:09:55-07:00","id":988859,"title":"","content":"When you say that you have reread the rules, please give a book and page for reference so everything can see the section that you are referencing to. The primary concern with using silver weapons is resource allocation, silver ammunition is difficult to acquire and silver ammunition is expensive to use. Silver ammunition should be saved for special circumstances, when the target is absolutely guaranteed to be Garou, and not for everyday use, as silver ammunition would take weeks to deliver after an order and, even if you have the required skills, would take hours to make per clip. <br /> <br /> If you have a character that is a hunter, how can your character tell the difference between a vampire or a werewolf? Most werewolves are primarily active at night and some vampires can change shape. If I am an ST with players that are hunters that fill their guns with silver ammunition and tend to shoot first and ask questions later, I will be making sure that they have plenty of encounters with vampires. I imagine that the players will be wondering if the entity that they shot just looks pissed rather than dropping dead from silver poisoning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T09:38:49-07:00","id":988893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luis Carlos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/974046-how-to-justify-enemys-not-having-silver-weaponry?p=988792#post988792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have readen the rules, and bullets covered with silver can hurt, but all weapons covered with silver lose it after a couple of hits. Garous also can be hurt with natural weapons of supernatural enemies (fangs, claws, horns, spikes...). And Pentex can raise a &quot;farm&quot; of poisonous &quot;pokemons&quot;.<br /> <br /> Other option is ordinary agentes to be equipped with &quot;special weapons&quot; like bullets of &quot;frozen poison&quot; or &quot;poisonous ice&quot; but they don't know they are using &quot;technomagic&quot;,</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly when you're talking about government agencies and private corporations with access to expansive R&amp;D divisions, their own production facilities, and more likely than not hedge mages and maybe a dynamic mage or two on-staff, the traditional rules fly straight out the window which make pushing the conversation in that direction something of a fool's errand. I mentioned that 3-4 pages ago myself, making up a hypothetical of making HEAT rounds that could be fired from 12-ga shotguns.<br /> <br /> Ever hear of Georgi Markov? He was a Bulgarian Cold War expatriate, and defector from the Eastern Bloc. One day, waiting for the bus, he felt a sharp sting on his leg and assumed he had been bitten by a bug. Four days later, he was dead of ricin poisoning; he'd been shot in the leg with a pellet specifically engineered to deliver a delayed, but lethal, dose of the toxin, via an air gun designed to look like an umbrella, by a Bulgarian secret police agent who'd infiltrated the United Kingdom.<br /> <br /> That was real life. Consider that, and imagine the bullshit a group with the resources of Pentex or the Technocracy working through federal agencies could pull off. Really, when you're talking about organizations like that, the question instead becomes &quot;why do they <i>just</i> use silver weaponry and put themselves at risk of physical harm and/or death, and exposure to the public or rival organizations?&quot;.<br /> <br /> Hell, in a <i>VtM</i> game I played in which my PC was a Lasombra <i>antitribu</i> who ran a major PMC through a shell corporation, his &quot;elite security unit&quot; (i.e. ghouls in the know, trained to fight vampires using modern warfare and counter-insurgency tactics) were armed with a custom, proprietary, melee weapon specifically designed to fight supernatural creatures, which was Masquerade-friendly due to looking like a contemporary modified entrenching tool.<br /> <br /> It's honestly more productive to the conversation to assume street-level activities here, not supraorganizations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}